  </div>
</div>

<h3>DFlash: block-diffusion drafting for speculative decoding</h3>
<p><strong>DFlash</strong> <span class="paper-tag">arXiv:2602.06036</span> uses a diffusion drafter that emits an entire block of γ=16 tokens in one forward pass, then verifies them in parallel against the main model. Because block diffusion is itself a refine-until-good loop, it composes naturally with the looping idea. The result: <strong>6.08× speedup</strong> on GSM8K versus 2.75× for EAGLE-3 (Qwen3-8B), and a 5-layer DFlash drafter beats a 1-layer EAGLE-3 on latency. The combination of weight-shared looping <em>inside</em> the diffusion drafter is the obvious next synthesis — and as of July 2026, it's an open direction, not yet a paper.</p>

